{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1376281-a-little-confusion-with-base-damage-and-duration-chart","id":1376281,"title":"A little confusion with Base Damage and Duration chart","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-03-23T11:34:27-07:00","id":1376281,"title":"A little confusion with Base Damage and Duration chart","content":"&quot;Base Damage or Duration&quot; chart in corebook says that on 1 success you deal no damage - okay, to affect another Pattern you need at least two successes. Then 2 successes go to two levels of damage. Still okay, we went through threshold and deal two damage per success. But then 3 go to six levels of damage and after it &quot;Number of successes&quot; x2? Why not substracting one from successes? And how that chart works when healing oneself or quintessence channeling?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24212-mesmeroflife","name":"MesmerOfLife","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-23T13:49:46-07:00","id":1376304,"title":"","content":"Well, the chart essentially gives you (successes - 1) x 2 damage. I think it's a bit unclear wording. When it comes to healing or quintessence channeling, it works in pretty much exactly the same way - except it's healed health levels or drawn quintessence. It's all more simple than it seems <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Personally I also use the chart when it comes to Mage vs. other-Sphere counterspelling, contested rolls and the like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-23T14:09:58-07:00","id":1376309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1376281-a-little-confusion-with-base-damage-and-duration-chart?p=1376304#post1376304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the chart essentially gives you (successes - 1) x 2 damage. I think it's a bit unclear wording. When it comes to healing or quintessence channeling, it works in pretty much exactly the same way - except it's healed health levels or drawn quintessence. It's all more simple than it seems <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Except that chart gives Successes x2, not successes-1.<br /> And it's also said that affecting others Patterns is more difficult than yourself and requires at least one more successes. So it should be difference between healing yourself and someone else. But with that non-linear progression it becomes a little difficult to understand how good mage can heal themself with 2 successes. Two health as it said in the chart? Or it should be one degree easier so he can heal himself by 6?<br /> Or just sucesses x2 and get 4 health but there's no &quot;4 health&quot; in that chart cause of sudden non-linear progression.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24212-mesmeroflife","name":"MesmerOfLife","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}